dx docs - build, check, and serve the mdBook documentation site (non-mutating; --check validates without rendering)

build, check, and serve the mdBook documentation site (non-mutating; --check validates without rendering)

Usage: dx docs [--check] [--apply] [--serve [--port <n>] [--host <addr>] [--open]] [--here] [scope ...] [-- bazel-options ...]

Arguments:
  [TARGETS]...
          Scopes to run on

  [BAZEL_OPTIONS]...
          Args after --

Options:
      --workspace <WORKSPACE>
          Use this workspace dir

      --dry-run[=<DRY_RUN>]
          Show the plan without running it. =false turns off an inherited default
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --quiet[=<QUIET>]
          Hide summaries. =false turns off an inherited default
          
          [possible values: true, false]

  -v, --verbose[=<VERBOSE>]
          Show more logs. =false turns off an inherited default
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --color <COLOR>
          Set color output

      --log-level <LEVEL>
          Set log level

      --output <OUTPUT>
          Set output format

      --bazel-startup-option <TOKEN>
          Select the Bazel server with --output_base=<path> or --output_user_root=<path>

      --check
          Check without changing files

      --apply
          Authorize the managed mutation or effect

      --here
          Use the current dir tree
          
          [alias: --cwd]

      --serve
          Serve docs locally

      --port <PORT>
          Docs serve port

      --host <HOST>
          Docs serve host

      --open
          Open docs in a browser

  -h, --help
          Print help

Per-command flags: --check/--serve/--port/--host/--open (docs only; `-- --bazel-options` pass through to the docs build; --check validates the book without rendering it, --serve previews the last build locally, --port/--host/--open require --serve; --output text|json only, diff has no patch). --apply authorizes rendering and serving.

Scopes: explicit Bazel labels/patterns (//..., //pkg:target, @repo//...), or workspace-relative files/dirs resolved via Bazel query. Bare scope selects the repository docs site (//docs/site:user_site, //docs/site:user_site_check in --check). Pass --here (--cwd alias) for the current directory tree instead (//path/...; //... at the root); --here cannot be combined with explicit scopes and never changes the no-flag default.
Exit codes: 0 success; 2 usage/scope/owner errors; 1 operational failures; Bazel-authoritative failures preserve Bazel's code.
Output: --output text|json; --report has no standard format for this command.
Rejected: --report, --fail-on, --min-coverage, --debug, --release, --bazel, --prune-unobserved, --pin, --rollback, --configured, --from, --to, --offline.
Environment: RUST_LOG=<filter> overrides --verbose and --log-level; NO_COLOR=<any> disables color; BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY=<dir> sets the workspace start. `dx --help` lists every DX_ default.

